course: dictionary
lesson: 15047
title: Taken back or pulled in
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word retracted comes from retract, which means to pull back in or to take back. Its meaning depends on what is being pulled or taken back, so look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: A cat can pull its claws back inside its paws. «The cat's claws were retracted, so the sofa was safe.» The sofa is the clue: the claws were hidden, so they could not scratch it.
explain: A person can also retract something they said. «Mia retracted her unkind words and said sorry.» The word sorry is the clue: Mia admits her words were wrong and takes them back.
fact: Retracted is the past form of retract, so it describes something that has already happened.
fact: «Retracted» means pulled back in, as with a cat's claws or a tortoise's head.
fact: «Retracted» can also mean took back something said or written, admitting it was wrong.
fact: In science, a retracted paper is one that has been officially taken back because it had mistakes.
fact: A good check is to swap in "pulled back in" or "taken back" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The cat's claws were retracted, so the sofa was safe.» What does retracted mean here? | Sharpened and ready to scratch | Painted bright red | *Pulled back in | Lost in the garden
exercise: Ben said his friend was a cheat. Then he saw the proof was wrong, so he retracted it. What did Ben do? | Said it again, louder | *Took back what he said, admitting it was wrong | Shouted at his friend | Wrote a book about it
exercise: «The scientists retracted their study after they found mistakes.» What happened to the study? | *It was officially taken back | It was read by a million people | It was printed in a bigger book | It was finished early
test: «The tortoise retracted its head into its shell when the dog barked.» Where did its head go? | Onto the dog | Out of the garden | *Inside its shell | Under the table
test: «Mia retracted her promise to share her sweets, so her brother felt let down.» What did Mia do to her promise? | Told everyone about it | *Took it back | Kept it safe in a box | Made it bigger
exam: «The news site retracted the story when it found the facts were false.» What does retracted suggest? | Made longer | Printed twice | *Officially taken back | Read aloud on the radio
